    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Facing a key personnel breakdown, the disordered contenders dismissed their head coach in a preemptive leadership purge with eight regular-season games left. The order-installing coach, John Tortorella, was brought in to restore stability, and his guidance was immediate. He imposed a winning regime, leading the NHL team to a 7-0-1 record to close the season and then guiding them through playoff runs. This organizational decision proved masterful, culminating in an authoritative series closure as the victors completed a four-game sweep in the Western Conference Final.",
